<title>UK: Iraq tells OPEC it pumped 1.019 mbpd in December.</title>
<headline>Iraq tells OPEC it pumped 1.019 mbpd in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq told OPEC it produced 1.019 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in December, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Iraq's December output, boosted from the middle of the month by its first exports in six years, rose 294,000 bpd from the 725,000 bpd Baghdad said it pumped in November.</p>
<p>Under a United Nations oil-for-food exchange Iraq is permitted to sell $2 billion worth of crude over six months to pay for humanitarian supplies.</p>
<p>Iraq's first exports left its Turkish pipeline outlet at Ceyhan on the Mediterranean on December 16.</p>
<p>Over the second half of December the Iraqi exports would amount to almost 600,000 bpd.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
